SWEET THERMAL (patch 0336, ALL-ON safety, user 2026-11-12: battery 51.6-53 C under stress with no throttle; facts: docs/research/150-thermal-path.md). A kernel thread on every boot (boot-arg sweetthermal=0 turns it off, default on) samples the MAX77759 fuel-gauge battery temperature (FG 0x36 reg 0x08, the read patch 0307 added to the SWEET CHG MON rows, no new register) and FG Current (0x0a) every 10 s through the existing HSI2C12 engine of sweet_chg_i2c.c, independent of USB and of every job (the engine is loaded for it even without sweetchgi2c=1; charger phase 1 is driven from the thread after 60 s when the USB log thread never did; a try-lock serialises the two callers). Prints `SWEET THERMAL: batt T C state S` on every state change and once per 60 s. Feeds iOS: IOPMPowerSource Temperature = the real value (centi-C, Estimated flag cleared; stale/no sample keeps the old flag + GAP) and SweetHIDTemperature (Product TG0B, ProductID 0x54473042, usage page 0xff00 usage 5, IOHIDEvent temperature events) for thermalmonitord. Kernel backstop (does not depend on iOS), table in bsd/dev/sweet_thermal.h: >= 48.0 C drop the X1 cores (sched_perfcontrol_update_recommended_cores 0x18, the patch 0270 call) [DEPENDENCY: mask 0x18 = logical cpu3,4 = the physical A76 pair only under tools/xrun's /cpus order 0,6,7,4,5,1,2,3 (applied when no --adt is given) with cpus=5, the order patch 0270's sweetrecores=0x1e assumes; the start of the thread reads the physical core of every logical cpu from the topology and prints one SWEET THERMAL line when it holds, else a GAP (cpus != 5, /cpus order differs, topology unavailable); the backstop stays active, the mask can never be empty], restore the boot mask at <= 44.0 C; >= 45.0 C while charging (FG current > 0) CNFG_09 back to its original value (the 0287 restore: same register, same value) until <= 42.0 C, then 875 mA again (only while the 0287 raise stands; the raise-again direction is bounded to THERM_MAX_WRITES = 16 per boot and then refused with a GAP while the bus stays alive, a hold (the lowering) is never refused by that bound so the final state is 500 mA; release only with the SuperSpeed link + CHGTYP; a hold that failed is asked again at the next sample, at most 4 times, a closed charger gate counts as busy); >= 55.0 C on two samples in a row: `SWEET THERMAL CRIT` and the orderly clean-stop + reset-to-bootloader (sweet_restart.c, the remote-reset path). A failed or implausible read (outside -20..90 C) is a GAP and takes NO action. GAP lines at boot for what note 150 says stays unknown (sensor->hotspot mapping, iOS CPU/GPU clamps have no backend, no ACPM client). Rule-8 items: (1) CNFG_09 hold/release on temperature = NEW trigger of the existing 0287 write (sweet_chg_icl_thermal -> i2c_cnfg09_write); (2) the HSI2C12 transfer-register writes and FG reads now happen on every boot (were: only sweetchgi2c=1); (3) CRIT = a new trigger of the existing PMU SMC mode write + software reset. The cores mask, the IOPMPowerSource value and the HID service are not hardware writes. Tests: tools/test_sweet_thermal.py. ORDER: applies AFTER patch 0333 (fix/wdt-early): the sweet_restart.c hunk 1 has 0333's `extern void sweet_wdt_stop_pets(void);` line in its context; tools/xnu-local-build skips a patch that does not git-apply, tools/test_sweet_thermal.py test_applies_after_0333 checks the order. Rule-8 review fixes (docs/reviews/0336-thermal-review.md): F1 bound on the raise direction only + refusal keeps the bus; F2 the first thermal transfer runs the pending-transfer checks of the P2 first group (i2c_gate(first)); F3 closed gate = busy (retried), failed hold retried bounded; F5 phase 1 never opened the gate = NOENGINE (sweet_chg_gate_established), no GAP per sample; F6 sweet_chg_tick(1); F7 cpu-order check; F8 release/acquire publish. TEST ONLY boot-arg sweetthermalramp=<deciC per sample> (1..100, user 2026-11-13): from the 3rd good sample on the state machine sees the real FG temperature + ramp * (good samples since the start), so a proof boot shows the X1 drop, the charge hold and the CRIT park without heating the battery; the value published to iOS (IOPMPowerSource Temperature, HID TG0B) stays the REAL sensor value; refused (GAP) outside 1..100, with sweetthermal=0, and per sample while the sensor read fails; every sample line prints "real T C, test bias +B C". A hot battery that is not charging says "not charging, nothing to hold".
